 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Sensing",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The LED (pins 1, 2) and the phototransistor (pins 3, 4) look out of two windows on one face. With nothing reflective in front the collector carries at most 1 µA; a surface in front returns the LED's light and the current rises. Response peaks with the reflector about 0.5 to 0.7 mm from the face and falls away beyond that: at 5 mm a white-paper target gives under a tenth of the peak current."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current grades",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "IC(ON) is specified with 20 mA in the LED, 5 V across the transistor and a mirror 1 mm away. QRE1113 and QRE1113GR guarantee 0.10 mA minimum (0.90 mA typical); QRE1114GR holds it between 0.30 and 0.60 mA. With no reflector, cross-talk through the package stays at or under 1 µA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Speed",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Rise and fall times depend on the load resistor: about 20 µs typical at 100 µA into 1 kΩ, and roughly 60 to 90 µs with RL = 10 kΩ at VCC = 10 V. Below about 3 kΩ the 0.3 mA curves are slower than the 1 mA curves; near 10 kΩ the four curves lie close together."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Dark current climbs roughly two decades between 25 °C and 85 °C. LED forward voltage falls slowly as temperature rises."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Reflow peaks at 260 °C for no more than 10 s, with at most 60 s above 220 °C and a pre-heat dwell at 180 °C to 200 °C of up to 120 s; ramps are 1 °C to 5 °C per second. Hand soldering is 240 °C for 5 s at 1.6 mm from the body; flow soldering 260 °C for 10 s."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Storage and moisture",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The leads are silver plated; long exposure to room air can oxidize them and degrade solderability. Parts outside their sealed packaging go back into a sealed moisture-barrier bag with desiccant, or into a dry cabinet held under 5% relative humidity. Assembled boards are stored the same way; a mounted part left in room air for a long time can suffer moisture damage in later high-temperature processing. Handling of these dry-packed parts is covered by onsemi application note AND8003/D."
  }
 ],
